Build a sustained study that joins representative feed/material identification, a defined reaction, time/thermal observations, product isolation and independent chemical/physical characterization. Choose actual appropriate primary methods, facilities and supervision for the chemistry; a literature or supplied-data version must identify that scope accurately.

Calibrate and test the consequential measurements, preserving blanks, sampling support, recovery, uncertainty and relevant instrument dynamics. Independently close material and energy where supported by the observations. Distinguish disappearance of feed, formation of desired product, isolated yield and accepted material state.

Test at least one consequential changed condition and a competing explanation for the result. Repeated or complementary observations should establish more than an isolated favorable sample. Trace cleaning, contamination, retained material and the actual time/history of the evidence.

**Work:** produce a complete primary-method account, original calculations and observation record with full external bibliography and data provenance. Have another reader reproduce a central inference and challenge the strongest alternative mechanism or measurement explanation. Revise the conclusions and explain which further process/scale claims the study does and does not establish.

